1
00:00:42,960 --> 00:00:47,965
THE PERFECT LIE

2
00:00:53,053 --> 00:00:54,638
THIS DRAMA IS A WORK OF FICTION

3
00:00:54,721 --> 00:00:57,975
SCENES INVOLVING CHILD ACTORS
AND ANIMALS WERE FILMED SAFELY

4
00:01:00,143 --> 00:01:03,188
Of the two of you, the one who lied…

5
00:01:05,607 --> 00:01:07,067
…is you.

6
00:01:12,614 --> 00:01:13,865
But…

7
00:01:16,159 --> 00:01:17,160
you said yourself

8
00:01:18,120 --> 00:01:20,581
that lie detector results
aren't always accurate.

9
00:01:23,208 --> 00:01:25,252
Are you questioning
the accuracy of the test?

10
00:01:25,335 --> 00:01:27,296
If you're unstable or extremely…

11
00:01:28,880 --> 00:01:30,132
extremely…

12
00:01:31,758 --> 00:01:35,345
extremely tired, the results can be wrong.
You said that yourself.

13
00:01:35,429 --> 00:01:36,930
I took a sedative that day,

14
00:01:37,848 --> 00:01:39,683
so I wasn't thinking clearly.

15
00:01:40,434 --> 00:01:42,436
That sounds a lot like your statement.

16
00:01:42,519 --> 00:01:44,646
That your memory was hazy from drinking.

17
00:01:50,068 --> 00:01:51,653
I'll take it again. Please.

18
00:02:05,334 --> 00:02:07,085
Please don't let Min Junho know.

19
00:02:07,169 --> 00:02:09,421
You said it can't be used
as evidence anyway.

20
00:02:17,804 --> 00:02:21,433
Everything from the investigation
is documented in the police case file.

21
00:02:22,225 --> 00:02:24,561
We also have to inform Mr. Min
of the results.

22
00:02:25,854 --> 00:02:29,441
This case will most likely be closed
without charges due to lack of evidence.

23
00:02:31,318 --> 00:02:33,236
It is quite likely…

24
00:02:35,113 --> 00:02:37,366
that you'll have to
pay the price for lying.

25
00:02:44,456 --> 00:02:46,083
No, wait. I…

26
00:02:54,675 --> 00:02:58,136
ANALYSIS INDICATED
DECEPTIVE RESPONSES IN EXAMINEE

27
00:02:58,220 --> 00:02:59,513
Damn it.

28
00:03:02,724 --> 00:03:05,394
No, wait… Damn it.

29
00:03:05,477 --> 00:03:11,650
EPISODE 3
TWO FACES

30
00:03:12,901 --> 00:03:13,902
[attorney] From what I can tell,

31
00:03:14,903 --> 00:03:17,114
she isn't going to let this go easily.

32
00:03:17,906 --> 00:03:19,616
-[cork pops softly]
-She'll take this all the way.

33
00:03:21,535 --> 00:03:22,786
And if she does?

34
00:03:22,869 --> 00:03:29,501
[attorney] The ones who've done it before
know how to play the game.

35
00:03:30,043 --> 00:03:34,172
She knows how to pressure a man
to get money out of him.

36
00:03:35,298 --> 00:03:37,092
She never mentioned money, though.

37
00:03:37,175 --> 00:03:42,681
Once she drags you all the way down,
you'll end up paying just to make it stop.

38
00:03:42,764 --> 00:03:45,225
Then she'll go,
"When did I ever ask you for money?"

39
00:03:45,308 --> 00:03:48,562
And she'll take the money anyway,
declaring victory.

40
00:03:48,645 --> 00:03:50,564
That's how the pros do it.

41
00:03:51,982 --> 00:03:55,444
But once the investigation is over,
there's nothing she can do, is there?

42
00:03:55,527 --> 00:03:58,280
[scoffs] You naive, clueless doctor.

43
00:03:58,947 --> 00:04:01,324
You think it's over
just because the cops cleared you?

44
00:04:02,325 --> 00:04:05,412
Your reputation is the trial,
and rumors are the punishment, get it?

45
00:04:05,495 --> 00:04:08,039
Especially for someone like you
who's got so much to lose.

46
00:04:11,126 --> 00:04:15,130
[sighs] There must've been a reason
for her to misunderstand me.

47
00:04:17,257 --> 00:04:18,258
Have you lost it?

48
00:04:18,925 --> 00:04:22,095
What, do you like her or something?

49
00:04:22,179 --> 00:04:23,388
What misunderstanding?

50
00:04:23,472 --> 00:04:26,057
Get a grip. Your reputation
and your son are at stake here.

51
00:04:27,350 --> 00:04:28,351
Enough.

52
00:04:28,435 --> 00:04:30,645
Press charges for false accusation
and defamation.

53
00:04:30,729 --> 00:04:32,773
You have to see it through
until she gives up.

54
00:04:32,856 --> 00:04:34,816
Do we really have to go that far?

55
00:04:45,160 --> 00:04:46,745
You lied to me, didn't you?

56
00:04:48,747 --> 00:04:49,790
[Junho] I didn't.

57
00:04:50,540 --> 00:04:52,542
[attorney] Then what?
Does she have something on you?

58
00:04:57,464 --> 00:04:58,632
I guess she does.

59
00:04:59,466 --> 00:05:00,717
Okay. What is it?

60
00:05:01,635 --> 00:05:02,636
She's…

61
00:05:04,471 --> 00:05:05,555
a teacher.

62
00:05:06,097 --> 00:05:07,307
I know she's a teacher.

63
00:05:09,017 --> 00:05:10,060
At Hyunsoo's school.

64
00:05:12,437 --> 00:05:13,647
She's his teacher.

65
00:05:16,733 --> 00:05:17,984
Hyunsoo doesn't know yet.

66
00:05:18,777 --> 00:05:21,822
If he happens to find out,
it'll only hurt him more.

67
00:05:21,905 --> 00:05:24,074
[attorney] Man, that woman is scary.

68
00:05:24,157 --> 00:05:26,952
She's using your kid as leverage.
This was totally planned.

69
00:05:27,035 --> 00:05:28,870
Come on, that's enough.

70
00:05:31,790 --> 00:05:33,333
Just wait and see.

71
00:05:33,416 --> 00:05:36,837
From here on out, that woman is going to
play the victim for all it's worth.

72
00:05:37,379 --> 00:05:40,632
If you don't tie her hands legally,
you'll be the one who loses.

73
00:05:41,383 --> 00:05:43,426
Do you think I'm lying too?

74
00:05:43,510 --> 00:05:44,678
[Jieun] No, but…

75
00:05:46,638 --> 00:05:48,640
I think it might be better to stop here.

76
00:05:49,641 --> 00:05:52,811
You want me to admit I lied? Now?

77
00:05:52,894 --> 00:05:55,730
-What if you misunderstood something?
-Misunderstood?

78
00:05:55,814 --> 00:05:57,732
You'd been drinking when it happened,

79
00:05:57,816 --> 00:06:00,026
so maybe you don't
remember everything clearly.

80
00:06:00,110 --> 00:06:01,736
Maybe that's why this says…

81
00:06:01,820 --> 00:06:04,197
POLYGRAPH TEST RESULTS

82
00:06:05,448 --> 00:06:07,742
No, this is all a lie.

83
00:06:09,119 --> 00:06:11,288
Come on,
you have to get on with your life.

84
00:06:11,371 --> 00:06:14,082
How am I supposed to have a life
after he ruined me like this?

85
00:06:14,165 --> 00:06:15,417
So now what?

86
00:06:18,503 --> 00:06:21,172
I'm going to ask them
to reinvestigate everything.

87
00:06:21,756 --> 00:06:24,301
-Is that even possible?
-Not you talking like that too!

88
00:06:24,384 --> 00:06:28,096
Then what? Tell you to go all the way
without thinking about the consequences?

89
00:06:28,179 --> 00:06:30,348
I can't live with this
being swept under the rug!

90
00:06:30,891 --> 00:06:32,767
If this whole thing gets quietly buried,

91
00:06:32,851 --> 00:06:35,520
Min Junho will never even know
what he did wrong,

92
00:06:35,604 --> 00:06:37,522
and he'll laugh at me!

93
00:06:56,207 --> 00:07:00,045
EXAMINEE MIN JUNHO'S RESPONSES
WERE DETERMINED TO BE TRUTHFUL

94
00:07:01,546 --> 00:07:03,965
So now we know for sure.

95
00:07:06,343 --> 00:07:08,762
Those are just the polygraph results.

96
00:07:09,262 --> 00:07:11,056
The investigation isn't over yet.

97
00:07:12,265 --> 00:07:13,683
About Ms. Kang…

98
00:07:15,810 --> 00:07:18,897
Maybe there's something
wrong with her psychologically.

99
00:07:19,439 --> 00:07:20,523
I'm worried about her.

100
00:07:21,524 --> 00:07:24,069
But of course, I can't even begin
to describe the pain

101
00:07:24,152 --> 00:07:25,737
and suffering I've been through.

102
00:07:26,529 --> 00:07:28,239
I don't know what to say.

103
00:07:30,241 --> 00:07:32,577
I don't know if I can ever trust someone…

104
00:07:34,913 --> 00:07:36,331
wholeheartedly again.

105
00:07:38,416 --> 00:07:40,585
We'll be wrapping up the case soon.

106
00:07:43,004 --> 00:07:44,839
What's really unfortunate is…

107
00:07:47,759 --> 00:07:49,511
because of people like Ms. Kang,

108
00:07:51,096 --> 00:07:53,390
actual victims may end up
staying silent out of fear

109
00:07:54,015 --> 00:07:58,353
that they'll be doubted
and falsely accused like this.

110
00:08:04,067 --> 00:08:05,568
Well, I'll see you soon.

111
00:08:17,747 --> 00:08:18,790
[doctor 1] Hey, Dr. Min!

112
00:08:20,458 --> 00:08:21,918
Looking for another hospital?

113
00:08:22,502 --> 00:08:26,339
Man, what happened to our star doctor?

114
00:08:28,216 --> 00:08:29,384
Take it easy.

115
00:08:30,885 --> 00:08:32,846
[doctor 2] What a scumbag.

116
00:08:42,439 --> 00:08:46,026
FROM SANGCHEON POLICE STATION
WOMEN &amp; JUVENILE AFFAIRS DIVISION

117
00:08:59,664 --> 00:09:01,583
Could I see the director for a moment?

118
00:09:03,209 --> 00:09:05,295
The foundation board members
are here with him,

119
00:09:05,378 --> 00:09:07,922
so you'll have to come back
after making an appointment.

120
00:09:09,924 --> 00:09:10,925
Oh.

121
00:09:38,495 --> 00:09:40,330
Could you just give him this?

122
00:09:40,413 --> 00:09:42,791
Sure. If you leave it here,
I'll give it to him later.

123
00:09:43,875 --> 00:09:44,876
I'll wait.

124
00:10:02,393 --> 00:10:06,773
EXAMINEE MIN JUNHO'S RESPONSES
WERE DETERMINED TO BE TRUTHFUL

125
00:10:50,608 --> 00:10:53,069
[aide] <i>Min Junho came to see</i>
<i>the director on his own.</i>

126
00:10:54,529 --> 00:10:55,572
[staff 1] <i>Gross.</i>

127
00:10:56,573 --> 00:10:58,032
<i>Is he handing in his resignation?</i>

128
00:10:58,741 --> 00:11:01,744
<i>Look at him coming back here</i>
<i>after getting hauled away in handcuffs.</i>

129
00:11:01,828 --> 00:11:03,121
<i>He's got some nerve.</i>

130
00:11:03,204 --> 00:11:05,456
[aide] <i>He brought his polygraph results.</i>

131
00:11:05,540 --> 00:11:06,541
[staff 1] <i>What's that?</i>

132
00:11:07,041 --> 00:11:08,042
[aide] <i>A lie detector.</i>

133
00:11:09,210 --> 00:11:11,671
<i>It says he wasn't lying.</i>
<i>Looks like he got played by a gold digger.</i>

134
00:11:11,754 --> 00:11:14,215
[gasps] No way.

135
00:11:15,508 --> 00:11:16,801
-What is it?
-[staff 2] Well,

136
00:11:16,885 --> 00:11:19,304
it looks like Dr. Min
got played by a gold digger.

137
00:11:19,888 --> 00:11:21,014
No way…

138
00:11:21,097 --> 00:11:22,390
What are you talking about?

139
00:11:22,891 --> 00:11:23,892
-Where?
-[staff 2] Look.

140
00:11:23,975 --> 00:11:25,602
[aide] <i>I guess she filed a false report.</i>

141
00:11:26,436 --> 00:11:27,562
[staff 3] <i>To extort money from him?</i>

142
00:11:28,062 --> 00:11:30,440
[staff 4] <i>So it was a false accusation.</i>
<i>That's crazy.</i>

143
00:11:30,523 --> 00:11:33,526
[staff 2 gasps] <i>I feel so bad for Dr. Min.</i>

144
00:11:33,610 --> 00:11:36,613
[staff 3] <i>See? I told you Dr. Min</i>
<i>would never do something like that.</i>

145
00:11:43,953 --> 00:11:44,954
[aide] Yes.

146
00:11:46,247 --> 00:11:47,248
Yes, okay.

147
00:11:54,505 --> 00:11:57,967
The director says you can come in now.

148
00:11:58,509 --> 00:11:59,510
Okay.

149
00:12:01,721 --> 00:12:04,515
[staff sighs] I feel so bad for him.

150
00:12:14,651 --> 00:12:15,985
-[thuds]
-Oh, my gosh.

151
00:12:19,405 --> 00:12:21,157
[director] Hey, Professor Min.

152
00:12:21,241 --> 00:12:23,034
You came without an appointment?

153
00:12:23,117 --> 00:12:26,037
I'm sorry. I was just going to drop off
the report and leave.

154
00:12:26,120 --> 00:12:29,165
Well, since you're here,
you might as well meet everyone.

155
00:12:30,124 --> 00:12:34,754
Everyone, this is Professor Min Junho,
one of the country's top cardiac surgeons.

156
00:12:34,837 --> 00:12:37,840
We get tons of VIP patients
from China asking for him.

157
00:12:38,591 --> 00:12:40,468
He's our hospital's star doctor.

158
00:12:43,471 --> 00:12:45,765
SANGCHEON UNIVERSITY HOSPITAL
MIN JUNHO

159
00:12:45,848 --> 00:12:49,352
[Junho] I'm sorry for causing you concern.

160
00:12:50,728 --> 00:12:52,188
If I may explain…

161
00:12:54,190 --> 00:12:55,984
Well, there's really nothing to explain.

162
00:12:56,067 --> 00:12:58,903
I just went on a normal date,

163
00:12:59,737 --> 00:13:01,572
and somehow it turned into all this.

164
00:13:02,448 --> 00:13:05,910
Well, you've certainly paid the price
for being famous.

165
00:13:05,994 --> 00:13:08,329
You have to be careful of people.

166
00:13:10,540 --> 00:13:12,542
I wasn't careful enough.

167
00:13:13,835 --> 00:13:15,670
So is the police investigation over now?

168
00:13:17,755 --> 00:13:20,008
There's nothing more
for them to investigate,

169
00:13:20,675 --> 00:13:22,427
so I think it's safe to say it is.

170
00:13:22,927 --> 00:13:26,180
Government agencies always take
their sweet time with these things.

171
00:13:27,390 --> 00:13:30,893
You know our VIP Cardiovascular Center
is opening later this year.

172
00:13:31,477 --> 00:13:33,104
You should join us, Professor Min.

173
00:13:34,981 --> 00:13:37,150
What would I be doing if I joined?

174
00:13:37,233 --> 00:13:39,360
Just keep doing what you're doing.

175
00:13:40,069 --> 00:13:43,448
We'll screen the patients,

176
00:13:43,531 --> 00:13:47,201
so all you need to do
is maintain your reputation.

177
00:13:50,496 --> 00:13:54,292
I don't know about my reputation,
but I'll make sure I keep my skills sharp.

178
00:13:56,169 --> 00:13:58,504
Thank you for trusting me.

179
00:13:58,588 --> 00:14:00,631
[chuckles] No need to thank me.

180
00:14:01,924 --> 00:14:05,470
But I don't trust you, sir.

181
00:14:07,889 --> 00:14:09,265
What are you talking about?

182
00:14:10,433 --> 00:14:12,435
You took me off
all my surgeries and rounds

183
00:14:12,518 --> 00:14:14,437
before the investigation results were out.

184
00:14:15,646 --> 00:14:17,482
You were basically telling me to leave.

185
00:14:18,566 --> 00:14:21,360
If this were a private practice,
that would be one thing.

186
00:14:21,444 --> 00:14:22,820
But this is different.

187
00:14:24,489 --> 00:14:27,992
These days, both the Medical Association
and the Hospital Association…

188
00:14:28,076 --> 00:14:31,245
They take a dim view of such misconduct.

189
00:14:35,666 --> 00:14:39,962
So I committed misconduct.

190
00:14:46,928 --> 00:14:47,929
You little punk.

191
00:14:48,012 --> 00:14:51,265
Just because I call you "Professor,"
you think you can forget your place?

192
00:14:58,815 --> 00:15:01,109
[laughs] Geez, you little…

193
00:15:01,943 --> 00:15:05,738
Fine. I'll trust you no matter
what happens from now on,

194
00:15:05,822 --> 00:15:07,990
so quit acting all sulky, you punk.

195
00:15:09,200 --> 00:15:11,285
Then I'm taking my patients back.

196
00:15:11,369 --> 00:15:12,578
Suit yourself.

197
00:15:12,662 --> 00:15:14,789
-And I'm going back into surgery.
-Go ahead.

198
00:15:14,872 --> 00:15:16,499
Do whatever you want.

199
00:15:16,582 --> 00:15:17,583
Geez.

200
00:15:26,384 --> 00:15:27,385
Hello.

201
00:15:33,599 --> 00:15:35,059
-[nurse 1] Hello, Dr. Min.
-[nurse 2] Hello.

202
00:15:45,027 --> 00:15:46,028
Dr. Min Junho.

203
00:15:48,948 --> 00:15:50,032
What is it?

204
00:15:53,786 --> 00:15:54,912
"What is it?"

205
00:15:54,996 --> 00:15:57,498
Right. What is it? Well…

206
00:16:00,626 --> 00:16:02,378
Shut your mouth and listen carefully.

207
00:16:04,005 --> 00:16:05,006
Excuse me?

208
00:16:06,382 --> 00:16:08,801
I know everything Kang Jisun said is true.

209
00:16:11,387 --> 00:16:12,555
You disgusting bastard.

210
00:16:13,139 --> 00:16:16,684
You might think you got away with it,
but it won't be that easy.

211
00:16:17,185 --> 00:16:18,186
Do you understand?

212
00:16:20,354 --> 00:16:21,772
Have a nice day.

213
00:16:23,816 --> 00:16:25,026
Mr. Park Junghyeon.

214
00:16:28,821 --> 00:16:32,575
I don't think I'm the one who needs
to watch out. You are.

215
00:16:33,159 --> 00:16:34,160
What?

216
00:16:36,871 --> 00:16:42,668
I know exactly what you've been doing
and with whom all this time.

217
00:16:51,510 --> 00:16:53,721
If you're going to have secret rendezvous,

218
00:16:53,804 --> 00:16:56,474
I suggest you pick a more
private location next time.

219
00:16:57,975 --> 00:17:00,269
There are plenty of empty rooms
around the hospital,

220
00:17:00,937 --> 00:17:02,563
but they're still public spaces.

221
00:17:05,691 --> 00:17:06,943
Have a nice day.

222
00:17:12,406 --> 00:17:14,617
-[indistinct chattering]
-[class bell rings]

223
00:17:26,504 --> 00:17:27,672
Who's not here?

224
00:17:27,755 --> 00:17:28,965
[student] Hyunsoo.

225
00:17:29,048 --> 00:17:30,049
Soyeon too.

226
00:17:32,009 --> 00:17:33,719
Does anyone know why they're late?

227
00:17:39,308 --> 00:17:40,434
Aren't you heading in?

228
00:17:44,730 --> 00:17:46,774
Is it because of what happened
with your dad?

229
00:17:49,527 --> 00:17:51,237
My dad didn't do anything wrong.

230
00:17:52,738 --> 00:17:54,115
Then why aren't you heading in?

231
00:17:55,700 --> 00:17:56,701
What about you?

232
00:18:00,204 --> 00:18:01,872
Let me borrow your account again.

233
00:18:06,335 --> 00:18:08,254
Why are you looking at me
like I'm pathetic?

234
00:18:14,677 --> 00:18:16,137
What's this supposed to get me?

235
00:18:17,013 --> 00:18:18,014
Then earn it yourself.

236
00:18:19,849 --> 00:18:21,058
[Soyeon] You're so annoying.

237
00:18:21,934 --> 00:18:23,019
Where are you going?

238
00:18:23,102 --> 00:18:24,103
[Hyunsoo] The bell rang.

239
00:18:28,190 --> 00:18:29,609
Hey, Kim Soyeon!

240
00:18:32,153 --> 00:18:33,988
-Hey!
-[Jisun] Oh, dear. Soyeon!

241
00:18:35,740 --> 00:18:37,158
What happened?

242
00:18:38,117 --> 00:18:40,620
Did you even know
what kind of pills they were?

243
00:18:42,496 --> 00:18:44,874
We have our monthly evaluation next week…

244
00:18:47,209 --> 00:18:48,753
and I haven't lost any weight.

245
00:18:53,299 --> 00:18:57,345
Those pills keep me from getting hungry.

246
00:18:59,055 --> 00:19:00,431
What?

247
00:19:00,514 --> 00:19:01,766
Where did you get them?

248
00:19:05,686 --> 00:19:08,064
Kids your age can't even get
a prescription for those.

249
00:19:08,147 --> 00:19:10,483
They're dangerous even for adults.
Now tell me.

250
00:19:12,485 --> 00:19:15,446
I won't take them ever again.

251
00:19:27,708 --> 00:19:29,210
Are you done with school?

252
00:19:32,171 --> 00:19:34,882
So you're asking me, your teacher,
to lie to your dad?

253
00:19:36,092 --> 00:19:38,219
[Soyeon] Please, Ms. Kang.

254
00:19:38,302 --> 00:19:42,181
If my dad finds out,
I'll be in so much trouble.

255
00:19:42,765 --> 00:19:45,851
-But still, I can't just--
-I can't quit being a trainee.

256
00:19:45,935 --> 00:19:48,771
Just tell him I fainted from anemia.

257
00:19:49,438 --> 00:19:52,441
I promise I'll never do it again.

258
00:19:52,942 --> 00:19:53,943
Please?

259
00:19:58,155 --> 00:20:00,116
Even if I lie for you,

260
00:20:01,158 --> 00:20:03,911
your dad's going to check with the doctor.

261
00:20:07,289 --> 00:20:10,543
Then I'll talk to my dad.

262
00:20:21,387 --> 00:20:23,097
<i>The call cannot be connected. Please…</i>

263
00:20:23,180 --> 00:20:26,434
ANESTHESIOLOGY

264
00:20:26,517 --> 00:20:27,935
-Hello.
-[nurse] Yes, hello.

265
00:20:28,018 --> 00:20:30,521
I'm a family member of Dr. Kang Jieun
in Anesthesiology.

266
00:20:30,604 --> 00:20:32,356
She's not answering her phone.

267
00:20:32,440 --> 00:20:34,692
Could you check
if she's in surgery right now?

268
00:20:34,775 --> 00:20:35,776
[nurse] One moment, please.

269
00:20:37,903 --> 00:20:41,282
Dr. Kang Jieun went into surgery
a little while ago.

270
00:20:42,616 --> 00:20:43,826
How long will it take?

271
00:20:44,744 --> 00:20:46,537
[nurse] At least five hours.

272
00:20:47,955 --> 00:20:48,956
[Jisun] Oh.

273
00:20:49,957 --> 00:20:51,208
Okay.

274
00:21:14,273 --> 00:21:17,943
Where do you see yourself in three years?

275
00:21:23,866 --> 00:21:26,577
First, I hope I'll have
a permanent teaching position.

276
00:21:28,245 --> 00:21:31,373
Then my life will be more stable
than it is now.

277
00:21:32,541 --> 00:21:37,630
And every school break,
I'll travel somewhere I love.

278
00:21:37,713 --> 00:21:43,093
Like, spending a month in Canada,
where <i>Anne of Green Gables</i> is set.

279
00:21:44,261 --> 00:21:45,262
[Junho] Hmm.

280
00:21:46,597 --> 00:21:48,349
What would you do there?

281
00:21:50,392 --> 00:21:51,936
Read <i>Anne of Green Gables</i> again?

282
00:21:55,272 --> 00:21:56,857
-That's cool.
-Sounds nice, right?

283
00:21:57,733 --> 00:21:59,568
-[Jisun laughs]
-What else?

284
00:22:01,987 --> 00:22:06,242
I'd also love to spend a whole month
surfing at Waikiki Beach in Hawaii.

285
00:22:06,325 --> 00:22:07,326
[Junho] Oh.

286
00:22:07,409 --> 00:22:09,453
I'd love to walk
the Camino de Santiago too,

287
00:22:09,537 --> 00:22:10,996
and if I get the chance,

288
00:22:11,080 --> 00:22:13,415
I'd like to see
the northern lights in Iceland.

289
00:22:17,378 --> 00:22:19,380
I hope you don't mind me asking, but…

290
00:22:21,423 --> 00:22:23,717
it sounds like
you haven't given much thought

291
00:22:24,426 --> 00:22:27,388
to sharing your life with someone.

292
00:22:30,266 --> 00:22:31,433
You mean, marriage?

293
00:22:39,942 --> 00:22:41,610
If I'm lucky, I guess.

294
00:22:45,948 --> 00:22:48,158
If I meet someone
I don't want to let go of.

295
00:22:53,080 --> 00:22:56,876
<i>You never know</i>
<i>what's around the corner in life.</i>

296
00:23:22,651 --> 00:23:24,486
Whatever Soyeon's circumstances are…

297
00:23:27,156 --> 00:23:28,741
it has nothing to do with Hyunsoo.

298
00:23:31,911 --> 00:23:35,164
And what exactly do we gain
by telling Soyeon's father the truth?

299
00:23:37,291 --> 00:23:40,252
Is it really right for a young student

300
00:23:40,336 --> 00:23:42,963
to lose her chance to pursue her dream
over one mistake?

301
00:23:46,008 --> 00:23:47,968
You got caught lying to me.

302
00:23:49,178 --> 00:23:50,888
And now you're asking me to lie too?

303
00:23:53,807 --> 00:23:56,769
I think she should take responsibility
for what she did.

304
00:23:58,228 --> 00:24:02,232
I don't want to teach her
to lie her way out

305
00:24:02,316 --> 00:24:06,070
of taking responsibility for her actions
like someone else I know.

306
00:24:07,947 --> 00:24:09,031
Excuse me?

307
00:24:09,114 --> 00:24:10,824
[Junho] Think about your own actions.

308
00:24:11,408 --> 00:24:13,744
What you did impulsively after drinking.

309
00:24:13,827 --> 00:24:15,287
Now you've suddenly turned on me.

310
00:24:15,371 --> 00:24:17,665
And you're trying to dump
all the blame onto me.

311
00:24:18,332 --> 00:24:19,333
Or…

312
00:24:22,169 --> 00:24:23,837
maybe there's something else you want.

313
00:24:29,760 --> 00:24:30,928
Mr. Min Junho.

314
00:24:33,389 --> 00:24:34,974
You can't fool me.

315
00:24:37,101 --> 00:24:40,145
On the outside, you're a successful man,
a respected doctor,

316
00:24:40,229 --> 00:24:42,398
and a father who seems
perfectly normal, but…

317
00:24:46,944 --> 00:24:47,945
on the inside…

318
00:24:49,405 --> 00:24:51,782
you're nothing but a despicable criminal.

319
00:24:58,539 --> 00:24:59,540
Jisun.

320
00:25:01,667 --> 00:25:02,668
I'm…

321
00:25:04,878 --> 00:25:07,006
not the kind of person you think I am.

322
00:25:10,175 --> 00:25:11,260
I'm really not.

323
00:25:36,493 --> 00:25:37,494
Soyeon!

324
00:25:42,916 --> 00:25:43,917
Are you okay?

325
00:25:44,001 --> 00:25:45,753
Don't worry. She's okay.

326
00:25:45,836 --> 00:25:48,797
Ms. Kang, what happened?

327
00:25:50,049 --> 00:25:52,092
-Well…
-[Soyeon's dad sighs]

328
00:25:52,176 --> 00:25:53,510
[Junho] Hello.

329
00:25:53,594 --> 00:25:55,512
Are you Soyeon's father?

330
00:25:56,221 --> 00:25:57,222
[Soyeon's dad] Yes.

331
00:25:57,306 --> 00:25:59,975
Well, it looks like Soyeon…

332
00:26:02,770 --> 00:26:05,230
may have pushed herself
a little too hard with practice.

333
00:26:06,315 --> 00:26:09,234
We ran some blood tests,
and nothing unusual came up.

334
00:26:09,318 --> 00:26:10,569
She's just exhausted.

335
00:26:11,487 --> 00:26:13,822
It can happen sometimes at her age.

336
00:26:15,616 --> 00:26:19,828
Luckily, her teacher here
took good care of her.

337
00:26:22,372 --> 00:26:23,373
[Soyeon's dad] Oh.

338
00:26:24,458 --> 00:26:26,001
-Thank you.
-[Jisun] Sure.

339
00:26:26,585 --> 00:26:28,796
[Soyeon's dad] Is there anything
we need to watch out for?

340
00:26:29,463 --> 00:26:32,174
She'll be fine after a few days
of rest and good food.

341
00:26:32,257 --> 00:26:34,885
Most importantly,
try to make sure she can relax.

342
00:26:35,469 --> 00:26:38,222
-[Soyeon's dad] Okay. Thank you.
-Of course.

343
00:26:39,014 --> 00:26:40,015
[Soyeon's dad] Geez.

344
00:26:40,516 --> 00:26:43,268
Why do you have to
make me worry like this?

345
00:26:44,019 --> 00:26:45,938
I told you not to overdo it.

346
00:26:46,647 --> 00:26:48,065
Seriously…

347
00:26:48,607 --> 00:26:50,567
Are you sure you feel okay?

348
00:26:51,110 --> 00:26:53,529
Look at you. Honestly.

349
00:26:58,450 --> 00:27:01,703
Getting out to the lineup isn't easy.

350
00:27:02,204 --> 00:27:05,290
You have to fight
through the smaller waves,

351
00:27:05,374 --> 00:27:08,710
dodge the big ones,
and keep paddling until you're out back.

352
00:27:09,545 --> 00:27:13,173
Today, we're going to learn
how to get through those bigger waves.

353
00:27:13,257 --> 00:27:14,675
It's called a duck dive.

354
00:27:15,968 --> 00:27:17,052
Shall we give it a try?

355
00:27:20,514 --> 00:27:21,974
<i>Just as the name suggests,</i>

356
00:27:22,057 --> 00:27:24,685
<i>you duck under the water like a duck</i>

357
00:27:24,768 --> 00:27:27,145
<i>to pass right beneath the wave.</i>

358
00:27:27,938 --> 00:27:29,273
<i>The most important thing is…</i>

359
00:27:30,440 --> 00:27:33,902
<i>you've got to dive under right as the wave</i>
<i>reaches its highest point.</i>

360
00:27:35,445 --> 00:27:37,531
<i>Go too early,</i>
<i>and you'll just get swept back.</i>

361
00:27:39,783 --> 00:27:40,784
<i>Go too late…</i>

362
00:27:46,248 --> 00:27:47,541
<i>…and you'll get flipped over.</i>

363
00:28:28,832 --> 00:28:31,168
-Are you having any discomfort?
-[patient] Not at all.

364
00:28:31,251 --> 00:28:33,253
I feel so much better now.

365
00:28:34,588 --> 00:28:37,925
Your biopsy results show
no signs of rejection,

366
00:28:38,008 --> 00:28:39,843
and your heart rate looks good too.

367
00:28:39,927 --> 00:28:41,136
The surgery went very well.

368
00:28:41,219 --> 00:28:44,514
My gosh, Dr. Min, you saved my life.

369
00:28:44,598 --> 00:28:47,184
You're a lifesaver!

370
00:28:47,267 --> 00:28:49,895
-You did great getting through surgery.
-[patient] Gosh, thank you.

371
00:28:55,192 --> 00:28:56,318
Hyunsoo.

372
00:29:02,074 --> 00:29:03,158
What's up?

373
00:29:06,870 --> 00:29:09,289
I wanted to talk to you.

374
00:29:12,584 --> 00:29:15,420
If it's not important, let's talk later.

375
00:29:16,004 --> 00:29:17,464
[Hyunsoo] Is it because of my dad?

376
00:29:24,137 --> 00:29:25,263
What do you mean?

377
00:29:28,350 --> 00:29:30,435
I thought we were friends,

378
00:29:32,104 --> 00:29:34,439
but I thought you might've changed
because of my dad.

379
00:29:36,525 --> 00:29:37,734
What are you talking about?

380
00:29:37,818 --> 00:29:39,069
My dad really didn't do it.

381
00:29:39,987 --> 00:29:42,030
The police said he was innocent.

382
00:29:42,114 --> 00:29:44,866
And a lie detector test
said he was telling the truth.

383
00:29:44,950 --> 00:29:47,160
They said that woman
approached him for his money.

384
00:29:49,746 --> 00:29:51,707
-Who told you that?
-My dad's the victim.

385
00:29:52,457 --> 00:29:54,334
-Wait…
-She's the one who did him wrong.

386
00:30:02,217 --> 00:30:03,468
Let's talk later…

387
00:30:06,263 --> 00:30:07,806
Let's talk about this another time.

388
00:30:15,188 --> 00:30:16,440
Hyunsoo.

389
00:30:23,989 --> 00:30:24,990
Never mind.

390
00:30:25,574 --> 00:30:26,825
I'll see you in class.

391
00:31:00,942 --> 00:31:02,778
-[guest] Oh, my gosh. I'm so sorry.
-[server] Are you okay?

392
00:31:02,861 --> 00:31:03,862
Sorry about that.

393
00:31:03,945 --> 00:31:06,698
-Let me get it for you.
-It slipped out of my hand. I'm sorry.

394
00:31:13,580 --> 00:31:14,664
Are you okay?

395
00:31:14,748 --> 00:31:19,836
Ah, I can't look at broken glass.

396
00:31:19,920 --> 00:31:22,255
It makes me picture
someone getting cut and bleeding.

397
00:31:25,550 --> 00:31:27,260
Doesn't seeing blood bother you?

398
00:31:30,180 --> 00:31:34,476
I can't let it bother me.
I am a doctor, after all.

399
00:31:37,062 --> 00:31:39,648
Do you try not to feel anything
if you can help it?

400
00:31:42,109 --> 00:31:44,319
It's more that

401
00:31:44,402 --> 00:31:49,908
I solemnly swore
to dedicate my life to serving humanity.

402
00:31:57,207 --> 00:31:59,042
So is there anything that scares you?

403
00:32:07,717 --> 00:32:09,678
[Junho] <i>Anything that scares me?</i>

404
00:32:14,599 --> 00:32:16,852
<i>After my wife passed away,</i>

405
00:32:16,935 --> 00:32:19,312
<i>Hyunsoo and I started living on our own.</i>

406
00:32:20,021 --> 00:32:22,232
Then one day, out of nowhere,

407
00:32:22,315 --> 00:32:24,442
we started hearing noises
outside the door.

408
00:32:25,527 --> 00:32:29,739
Hyunsoo said he thought
his mom wanted to come inside.

409
00:32:33,285 --> 00:32:36,830
We have this black horse statue
outside our place

410
00:32:36,913 --> 00:32:39,249
that my wife bought to protect the house.

411
00:32:40,208 --> 00:32:43,962
One day,
Hyunsoo put our house key under it.

412
00:32:45,213 --> 00:32:48,967
<i>And strangely enough,</i>
<i>we haven't heard the noises since.</i>

413
00:32:50,719 --> 00:32:53,221
[Junghyeon] <i>Drugs to commit a crime</i>
<i>and a wife dead from an overdose.</i>

414
00:32:53,305 --> 00:32:54,973
<i>Isn't that too much of a coincidence?</i>

415
00:32:56,016 --> 00:32:58,894
<i>If a medical professional is determined,</i>
<i>there's no stopping them.</i>

416
00:33:00,395 --> 00:33:03,857
<i>Who knows what kind of drugs that bastard</i>
<i>might have hidden in his house?</i>

417
00:33:07,277 --> 00:33:10,197
What does the surgery schedule
look like on Thursday?

418
00:33:11,448 --> 00:33:13,700
There's one scheduled for 11:30 a.m.

419
00:33:13,783 --> 00:33:15,452
Is that the earliest?

420
00:33:16,161 --> 00:33:19,206
-That's the earliest we have that day.
-[Junho] Hmm.

421
00:34:01,915 --> 00:34:07,420
DISPOSABLE SHOE COVERS

422
00:34:50,130 --> 00:34:52,257
Where did Yunji go?

423
00:34:52,924 --> 00:34:55,135
I brought her some chocolate.

424
00:34:57,137 --> 00:35:01,224
Well, no one's here, so I guess
I'll just have to eat it myself.

425
00:35:01,308 --> 00:35:03,393
No, you can't, Dr. Min!

426
00:35:05,895 --> 00:35:07,230
-Liar.
-[door slides]

427
00:35:07,314 --> 00:35:08,648
[Yunji's mom] Hello, Dr. Min.

428
00:35:09,357 --> 00:35:13,570
Ma'am, I think Yunji's the liar here.

429
00:35:13,653 --> 00:35:14,696
Look at this.

430
00:35:15,614 --> 00:35:19,159
She kept refusing to take her medicine,
so I bought her just one.

431
00:35:19,242 --> 00:35:21,077
So you're the culprit.

432
00:35:21,161 --> 00:35:23,204
Caught red-handed.

433
00:35:23,288 --> 00:35:25,832
Absolutely no more of these
until after the surgery.

434
00:36:49,916 --> 00:36:51,751
I guess he's unhappy with everything I do.

435
00:36:53,086 --> 00:36:55,547
He tells me not to use his birthday
as the door code,

436
00:36:55,630 --> 00:36:57,841
<i>not to make him breakfast without asking…</i>

437
00:36:59,968 --> 00:37:02,387
MIN, HYUNSOO
NOVEMBER 3, 2015

438
00:37:45,680 --> 00:37:47,891
Yunji's surgery is next week, right?

439
00:37:47,974 --> 00:37:49,142
[nurse] Yes, Thursday.

440
00:37:49,934 --> 00:37:52,771
Please make sure her blood sugar
stays under 140 mg.

441
00:37:53,354 --> 00:37:56,399
She's a child, so it'll probably be harder
to keep it under control.

442
00:37:56,900 --> 00:37:57,942
[nurse] Will do.

443
00:37:59,569 --> 00:38:01,571
You ended up staying late
because of Yunji.

444
00:38:03,156 --> 00:38:04,407
Well, she's my patient.

445
00:38:05,408 --> 00:38:06,451
See you tomorrow.

446
00:38:41,611 --> 00:38:43,780
[Junho] <i>We have this black horse statue</i>
<i>outside our place</i>

447
00:38:43,863 --> 00:38:45,698
<i>-that my wife bought to protect the house.</i>

448
00:38:46,282 --> 00:38:50,203
One day,
Hyunsoo put our house key under it.

449
00:39:43,798 --> 00:39:46,217
POSTAL DELIVERY

450
00:40:43,733 --> 00:40:44,859
30 MIN
26 KM

451
00:40:44,943 --> 00:40:48,655
<i>Sharp turn ahead. Please drive safely.</i>

452
00:41:32,615 --> 00:41:36,995
[radio host] <i>Meanwhile, strong winds</i>
<i>are expected in parts of the east coast,</i>

453
00:41:37,078 --> 00:41:40,206
<i>so secure any outdoor structures</i>
<i>and take extra care to avoid accidents.</i>

454
00:42:27,003 --> 00:42:29,047
[automated voice] <i>A vehicle has arrived.</i>

455
00:43:12,590 --> 00:43:13,591
Damn it.

456
00:44:26,330 --> 00:44:27,957
<i>Hello, this is the management office.</i>

457
00:44:28,040 --> 00:44:31,002
<i>We have some mail here for you,</i>
<i>so please come by to pick it up.</i>

458
00:44:53,357 --> 00:44:54,358
-[Jisun] Oh!
-[clattering]

459
00:45:17,256 --> 00:45:20,468
MAIL DELIVERY NOTICE
45 P.M.

460
00:46:26,617 --> 00:46:30,538
-Brad! Where are you going? Get back here!
-[dog barks]

461
00:46:31,664 --> 00:46:34,083
Oh, Dr. Min! Grab my dog, please!

462
00:46:35,084 --> 00:46:36,335
Hey, Brad!

463
00:46:36,961 --> 00:46:37,962
Darn it.

464
00:46:55,646 --> 00:46:57,064
[Junho] Hey, hold on.

465
00:46:59,817 --> 00:47:01,152
[laughs] Hey, why did you…

466
00:47:18,586 --> 00:47:20,212
I would've chased him around all day

467
00:47:20,296 --> 00:47:21,714
-if it weren't for you.
-[Junho] I know.

468
00:47:21,797 --> 00:47:23,549
How old is he?

469
00:47:23,632 --> 00:47:25,509
-[neighbor] He's turning five.
-[Junho] Gosh, you…

470
00:47:29,013 --> 00:47:31,891
-[neighbor] Isn't he handsome? [laughs]
-[Junho chuckles] You're so cute.

471
00:47:31,974 --> 00:47:34,101
He never listens to me. Honestly…

472
00:47:34,769 --> 00:47:35,895
I'll see you around.

473
00:47:35,978 --> 00:47:36,979
-[neighbor] Sure.
-[Junho] Okay.

474
00:47:37,063 --> 00:47:38,522
-[neighbor] Thank you so much.
-[Junho] No problem.

475
00:47:38,606 --> 00:47:39,857
-[neighbor] Have a good one.
-[Junho] Goodbye.

476
00:47:39,940 --> 00:47:40,983
[neighbor] See you around.

477
00:49:53,741 --> 00:49:54,742
Huh?

478
00:50:01,123 --> 00:50:03,042
[gasps] Where did it go?

479
00:50:15,387 --> 00:50:16,305
Damn it.

480
00:50:16,388 --> 00:50:17,431
[Hyunsoo] What's this?

481
00:50:18,349 --> 00:50:20,142
-Why?
-It's steak.

482
00:50:20,851 --> 00:50:22,144
Nice surprise, huh?

483
00:50:22,228 --> 00:50:23,270
Steak or people,

484
00:50:23,354 --> 00:50:25,773
it's nicest when they come out of nowhere.

485
00:50:25,856 --> 00:50:27,316
I'm not that excited.

486
00:50:27,399 --> 00:50:29,109
Say, "I love you, Dad," before you eat.

487
00:50:29,193 --> 00:50:30,861
Thanks for the food.

488
00:50:39,161 --> 00:50:40,496
[Hyunsoo] I wonder what's going on.

489
00:50:56,720 --> 00:50:58,055
What's going on?

490
00:50:58,138 --> 00:50:59,515
[detective] Mr. Min Junho?

491
00:50:59,598 --> 00:51:00,683
[Junho] Yes.

492
00:51:00,766 --> 00:51:02,017
I asked what's going on.

493
00:51:02,601 --> 00:51:04,353
[detective] We received a tip
about drug possession.

494
00:51:05,521 --> 00:51:06,939
A tip about drug possession?

495
00:51:26,208 --> 00:51:27,209
What's this?

496
00:51:28,877 --> 00:51:31,797
Wait, how did you know you'd find this?

497
00:51:40,639 --> 00:51:41,640
Hyunsoo.

498
00:51:42,182 --> 00:51:44,560
It's nothing.
There's been a misunderstanding.

499
00:51:44,643 --> 00:51:47,563
I'll be back soon, so don't worry.
Just go inside.

500
00:51:53,861 --> 00:51:55,279
Go on in, okay?

501
00:52:19,720 --> 00:52:21,180
Let me make a phone call.

502
00:52:44,495 --> 00:52:45,746
Hello?

503
00:52:45,829 --> 00:52:48,123
[caller] <i>Hello. Is this Ms. Kang Jisun?</i>

504
00:52:49,541 --> 00:52:50,542
Who is this?

505
00:52:52,336 --> 00:52:53,629
The police suddenly showed up

506
00:52:53,712 --> 00:52:55,839
after getting a report
and found medicine vials.

507
00:52:55,923 --> 00:52:57,591
-I'm on my way to the station now.

508
00:52:59,259 --> 00:53:00,552
Sangcheon Police Station.

509
00:53:04,598 --> 00:53:05,641
Okay.

510
00:53:12,773 --> 00:53:13,816
My lawyer.

511
00:53:19,697 --> 00:53:21,615
Who gave you the tip?

512
00:53:21,699 --> 00:53:26,078
<i>I'm afraid I can't disclose that</i>
<i>due to our policy of protecting sources.</i>

513
00:53:26,161 --> 00:53:27,788
<i>Why don't we meet and talk in person?</i>

514
00:53:27,871 --> 00:53:30,249
I don't want to do an interview
or anything like that.

515
00:53:30,332 --> 00:53:32,418
<i>This isn't just about you.</i>

516
00:53:32,501 --> 00:53:33,794
<i>There are many women like you</i>

517
00:53:33,877 --> 00:53:35,921
<i>-who get branded as gold diggers--</i>
-No, thanks.

518
00:53:40,759 --> 00:53:42,886
I knew this was going to happen to you.

519
00:53:42,970 --> 00:53:46,181
They say an anonymous woman
tipped them off. It's obvious who it was.

520
00:53:46,265 --> 00:53:47,266
[Junho] Who was it?

521
00:53:51,186 --> 00:53:54,815
Hey. You said that woman's claiming
she was drugged.

522
00:53:54,898 --> 00:53:58,444
So who do you think reported
that you had drugs in your house?

523
00:53:59,319 --> 00:54:00,487
There's no way…

524
00:54:00,571 --> 00:54:01,572
[attorney] Seriously?

525
00:54:01,655 --> 00:54:03,615
Geez, you really are naive and clueless.

526
00:54:04,658 --> 00:54:07,619
The police searched under the bed
as soon as they came in.

527
00:54:07,703 --> 00:54:08,829
They knew where to look.

528
00:54:08,912 --> 00:54:10,748
There's no way she could've known that.

529
00:54:11,331 --> 00:54:13,542
Those narcotics detectives
are bloodhounds.

530
00:54:13,625 --> 00:54:16,587
The second they walk into a place,
they know exactly where to look.

531
00:54:19,590 --> 00:54:21,592
Your neighbors saw you
get taken away, right?

532
00:54:24,261 --> 00:54:25,471
[Junho] Yeah.

533
00:54:25,554 --> 00:54:26,555
Hyunsoo saw too?

534
00:54:33,270 --> 00:54:35,606
This is just the beginning, okay?

535
00:54:36,231 --> 00:54:38,025
I told you, that woman's a pro.

536
00:54:38,650 --> 00:54:40,944
<i>She'll demand a reinvestigation,</i>
<i>file false reports,</i>

537
00:54:41,028 --> 00:54:43,864
<i>feed people false tips, spread rumors,</i>
<i>and take this all the way.</i>

538
00:54:47,826 --> 00:54:48,827
Still…

539
00:54:49,828 --> 00:54:51,497
I don't want to press charges.

540
00:54:53,123 --> 00:54:54,625
She's Hyunsoo's teacher.

541
00:54:56,752 --> 00:55:00,797
[attorney] Then let's at least
get a story out there, okay?

542
00:55:00,881 --> 00:55:02,299
I know a reporter.

543
00:55:02,382 --> 00:55:05,385
He loves sensational stuff
and lives for clicks.

544
00:55:05,469 --> 00:55:06,470
He's good.

545
00:55:08,055 --> 00:55:09,056
Come on.

546
00:55:09,139 --> 00:55:12,309
We need to get something in the press
to keep her in check.

547
00:55:12,392 --> 00:55:14,436
-Why won't you listen to me?
-[door opens]

548
00:55:15,938 --> 00:55:17,064
All done?

549
00:55:17,606 --> 00:55:20,067
[detective] Oh, here. Have one each.

550
00:55:21,318 --> 00:55:23,153
-No, thank you.
-[detective chuckles]

551
00:55:24,112 --> 00:55:28,033
Just sign here, and you're free to go.

552
00:55:28,116 --> 00:55:32,621
You had this so nicely tucked away,
you ended up coming for no reason.

553
00:55:34,122 --> 00:55:35,207
Can I go now?

554
00:55:35,290 --> 00:55:37,709
Yes. Don't forget to take
these insulin vials with you.

555
00:55:39,044 --> 00:55:40,337
Take care.

556
00:55:40,837 --> 00:55:41,922
-[attorney] Bye.
-Bye.

557
00:55:44,091 --> 00:55:45,551
Geez…

558
00:55:53,976 --> 00:55:55,811
QUASI-RAPE

559
00:55:55,894 --> 00:55:58,272
…NO CHARGES…

560
00:55:58,355 --> 00:56:01,441
…DECIDED NOT TO REFER THE CASE…

561
00:56:15,747 --> 00:56:17,040
Dad, are you okay?

562
00:56:31,513 --> 00:56:33,765
When your mom was pregnant with you,

563
00:56:34,474 --> 00:56:36,643
she had gestational diabetes.

564
00:56:38,395 --> 00:56:41,565
She was treated for it for a few years
even after you were born.

565
00:56:42,691 --> 00:56:46,778
I forgot to throw out some insulin vials
that were left over from back then.

566
00:56:48,614 --> 00:56:50,365
Did we bring them with us when we moved?

567
00:56:52,743 --> 00:56:55,078
I don't know.
I guess it came along with something.

568
00:56:56,538 --> 00:56:59,291
But that's not what's important.

569
00:57:00,876 --> 00:57:02,210
Then what is?

570
00:57:05,631 --> 00:57:06,882
You and me.

571
00:57:11,011 --> 00:57:14,723
On my way to the police station,
I realized something.

572
00:57:17,392 --> 00:57:21,688
When your mom was unwell,
I was so focused on her

573
00:57:22,689 --> 00:57:26,151
that I didn't give you enough hugs.

574
00:57:27,694 --> 00:57:30,364
So I figured
I'd better make up for it now.

575
00:57:30,947 --> 00:57:32,532
[Hyunsoo] Gross.

576
00:57:33,158 --> 00:57:37,120
Just deal with it.
I'm putting up with how gross this is too.

577
00:57:40,040 --> 00:57:41,041
[Hyunsoo] Dad.

578
00:57:41,958 --> 00:57:42,959
[Junho] Yeah?

579
00:57:46,672 --> 00:57:48,757
So something like that
will never happen again?

580
00:57:51,093 --> 00:57:52,094
[Junho] No.

581
00:58:07,609 --> 00:58:08,610
It's me.

582
00:58:09,361 --> 00:58:10,487
I changed my mind.

583
00:58:11,863 --> 00:58:13,699
Who's that reporter you mentioned?

584
00:58:14,616 --> 00:58:15,617
Oh, no.

585
00:58:15,701 --> 00:58:18,578
Another teacher tried to take their life
because of depression.

586
00:58:18,662 --> 00:58:20,664
The parents filed 14 complaints,

587
00:58:20,747 --> 00:58:22,999
claiming they violated
their child's rights.

588
00:58:23,083 --> 00:58:24,876
Don't follow the news.

589
00:58:24,960 --> 00:58:27,671
These days,
going online just makes you feel worse.

590
00:58:27,754 --> 00:58:28,755
For you.

591
00:58:28,839 --> 00:58:31,967
I really don't know what's happening
to the world these days.

592
00:58:32,050 --> 00:58:33,385
-[teacher 1] Tell me about it.
-[teacher 2] Goodness.

593
00:58:35,011 --> 00:58:36,930
Oh, my gosh. What is this?

594
00:58:37,013 --> 00:58:38,932
-[teacher 3] What is it?
-[teacher 1] Why? What is it?

595
00:58:42,686 --> 00:58:46,064
Damn, this is insane!

596
00:58:46,148 --> 00:58:48,024
Hey, check this out.

597
00:58:49,192 --> 00:58:50,235
-What is it?
-Let's see.

598
00:58:50,318 --> 00:58:52,154
-[Sanghyeon] Is this for real?
-[student] Isn't this our school?

599
00:58:52,237 --> 00:58:53,572
[Sanghyeon] Right?

600
00:58:53,655 --> 00:58:56,116
Looks like it, right?
This isn't fake news, is it?

601
00:58:59,703 --> 00:59:02,664
An elementary school in Sangcheon
that starts with S…

602
00:59:02,748 --> 00:59:03,790
Isn't that us?

603
00:59:03,874 --> 00:59:06,042
Forget the S.
We're the only prestigious school…

604
00:59:06,126 --> 00:59:07,627
Wait, let me see.

605
00:59:08,962 --> 00:59:11,548
All right, everyone. Take your seats.

606
00:59:12,299 --> 00:59:14,801
-[Sanghyeon] Ms. Kang, you're in the news.
-[student] Hey, don't…

607
00:59:15,343 --> 00:59:16,636
Me?

608
00:59:16,720 --> 00:59:18,972
[teacher 1] A contract Korean teacher?

609
00:59:19,055 --> 00:59:20,390
[teacher 2] Korean?

610
00:59:21,725 --> 00:59:23,185
Korean?

611
00:59:23,268 --> 00:59:25,812
The one that teaches
reading and writing. Ms. Kang!

612
00:59:26,605 --> 00:59:27,773
That's right.

613
00:59:28,565 --> 00:59:30,942
Ms. Kang, are you a gold digger?

614
00:59:31,026 --> 00:59:32,694
-[student] Hey.
-Hey, you can't say that.

615
00:59:32,778 --> 00:59:34,279
It says so right here.

616
00:59:38,033 --> 00:59:39,701
I didn't think she was like that.

617
00:59:42,537 --> 00:59:45,624
WOMEN WHO USE SEX AS A WEAPON,
SUSPICIOUS BEHAVIOR OF CONTRACT TEACHER

618
00:59:45,707 --> 00:59:47,125
That woman was you?

619
01:00:15,654 --> 01:00:16,696
[student 1] I guess it's true.

620
01:00:16,780 --> 01:00:18,114
-Hey, I guess it's really true.
-[student 2] Yeah.

621
01:01:22,095 --> 01:01:23,889
Looking for something?

622
01:01:23,972 --> 01:01:25,307
Oh.

623
01:01:25,390 --> 01:01:27,559
I came to drop off the notice.

624
01:01:31,980 --> 01:01:34,190
WOMEN &amp; JUVENILE AFFAIRS DIVISION

625
01:01:34,274 --> 01:01:36,359
Has a decision been made?

626
01:01:37,777 --> 01:01:38,778
Yes.

627
01:01:39,279 --> 01:01:42,616
We've decided not to refer the case
for prosecution due to lack of evidence.

628
01:01:50,206 --> 01:01:51,207
Then…

629
01:01:52,792 --> 01:01:54,169
it's over now.

630
01:01:55,712 --> 01:01:59,633
I apologize
for the inconvenience we've caused.

631
01:02:04,554 --> 01:02:06,640
Let me ask you one last question.

632
01:02:09,392 --> 01:02:11,144
What happened that night with Ms. Kang…

633
01:02:12,437 --> 01:02:13,521
Do you regret it?

634
01:02:16,191 --> 01:02:17,192
No.

635
01:02:17,692 --> 01:02:19,194
I didn't do anything wrong,

636
01:02:19,945 --> 01:02:21,237
so I have nothing to regret.

637
01:02:24,950 --> 01:02:25,951
Understood.

638
01:02:27,160 --> 01:02:29,996
I hope you don't find yourself
in a similar situation again.

639
01:02:33,083 --> 01:02:34,334
Goodbye.

640
01:02:37,087 --> 01:02:38,254
Wait, Detective.

641
01:02:46,429 --> 01:02:47,430
Never mind.

642
01:02:47,931 --> 01:02:48,932
What is it?

643
01:02:54,145 --> 01:02:55,397
If you're free,

644
01:02:56,439 --> 01:02:58,108
would you like to get a drink with me?

645
01:03:01,653 --> 01:03:02,654
Excuse me?

646
01:03:04,614 --> 01:03:05,615
[Junho] Every day…

647
01:03:06,908 --> 01:03:09,369
has been really hard for me lately.

648
01:03:10,912 --> 01:03:12,539
And today's been a long day too.

649
01:03:14,165 --> 01:03:17,002
I just don't feel like celebrating alone.

650
01:03:18,586 --> 01:03:21,047
And I wanted to thank you too--

651
01:03:21,131 --> 01:03:22,424
I'm on duty.

652
01:03:26,428 --> 01:03:27,721
I'll wait until you're off.

653
01:03:27,804 --> 01:03:29,514
I don't socialize…

654
01:03:32,600 --> 01:03:34,477
with people I've investigated.

655
01:03:40,025 --> 01:03:41,026
Okay.

656
01:03:44,070 --> 01:03:46,197
Well, then… Get home safe.

657
01:03:47,240 --> 01:03:48,241
Will do.

658
01:04:24,110 --> 01:04:28,031
THE PERFECT LIE

659
01:04:54,974 --> 01:04:56,101
[Jisun] <i>What about me?</i>

660
01:04:57,477 --> 01:04:58,478
YOU'RE FINISHED NOW!

661
01:04:59,020 --> 01:05:00,188
<i>What about my life?</i>

662
01:05:00,271 --> 01:05:02,899
[Junho] <i>Do you have any idea</i>
<i>what my son and I are going through?</i>

663
01:05:02,982 --> 01:05:04,567
[Jisun] <i>Call that reporter.</i>

664
01:05:04,651 --> 01:05:07,112
Tell them what you did
and how you covered it up.

665
01:05:07,195 --> 01:05:09,364
Please, just stop
with those ridiculous lies!

666
01:05:09,447 --> 01:05:10,615
I can't stop.

667
01:05:10,698 --> 01:05:12,492
[Hwayoung] <i>He's a very dangerous man.</i>

668
01:05:13,284 --> 01:05:16,329
It looks like someone broke into my house.

669
01:05:17,664 --> 01:05:19,791
[Jisun] <i>If I make it through those waves,</i>

670
01:05:20,458 --> 01:05:22,836
<i>will I be able</i>
<i>to get back to the starting point?</i>

671
01:05:39,144 --> 01:05:40,770
THE PERFECT LIE

672
01:05:40,854 --> 01:05:42,856
Translated by Liya Hyunjoo Choi
